---
import { ENTRIES, day, formatDuration, person } from '@lib/features/time-tracking';

const onBehalf = ENTRIES.find(entry => entry.loggedBy !== undefined);
if (!onBehalf?.loggedBy) throw new Error('The logged-for example needs an entry logged on someone’s behalf');
const onBehalfLine = [
  person(onBehalf.author).name,
  day(onBehalf.date).long,
  `${formatDuration(onBehalf.minutes)} ${onBehalf.workType}`,
  `logged by ${person(onBehalf.loggedBy).name}`,
].join(' · ');
---

<section class="border-t border-line bg-app" aria-labelledby="time-decision-title">
  <div class="wrap py-16 md:py-24 grid lg:grid-cols-12 gap-10 lg:gap-12">
    <div class="lg:col-span-5">
      <h2 id="time-decision-title" class="h2">
        On where it helps, off where it does not.
      </h2>
      <p class="prose mt-5 max-w-[46ch]">
        Time tracking is a setting on each project, on for a new one. A Project Admin can switch it off: Estimation and
        Spent time leave that project’s issues and nobody can log time there. Nothing is deleted, so switching it back
        on brings every record back.
      </p>
      <div class="mt-6 flex flex-col items-start gap-3 text-sm">
        <a class="link" href="/features/project-reports">
          The time report, timesheets and the other reports
          <span class="arr" aria-hidden="true">
            →
          </span>
        </a>
        <a class="link" href="/features/issue-tracking">
          Custom fields as your Estimation or Spent time
          <span class="arr" aria-hidden="true">
            →
          </span>
        </a>
      </div>
    </div>
    <div class="lg:col-span-6 lg:col-start-7 rule-list">
      <div class="py-6">
        <h3 class="h3">For learning.</h3>
        <p class="prose mt-2 text-base">
          Put an estimate on the issue and the sidebar shows what has been logged against it, turning red once it goes
          over. The time report puts estimate, spent and the difference side by side for every issue in scope.
        </p>
      </div>
      <div class="py-6">
        <h3 class="h3">For accountability.</h3>
        <p class="prose mt-2 text-base">
          Every addition, change and removal of a record is kept in the issue’s history. You edit or delete your own
          records; Project Admins can edit or delete anyone’s, and deleting asks first.
        </p>
      </div>
      <div class="py-6">
        <h3 class="h3">For client work.</h3>
        <p class="prose mt-2 text-base">
          Add a work item attribute such as <em>Billable</em>, group the time report by it, and export the same numbers
          to CSV. Each row still traces back to the issue the time was logged on.
        </p>
      </div>
      <div class="py-6">
        <h3 class="h3">Who logs for whom.</h3>
        <p class="prose mt-2 text-base">
          Contributors and above log their own time; Observers read it. Project Admins and organisation admins can log
          for any member who could log their own. The record shows who logged it and stays the author’s to edit.
        </p>
        <p class="quote mt-3">{onBehalfLine}</p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>
